👑🧠 Birbal and the Blind Man (Raw Story)

One day, Emperor Akbar asked Birbal, “How many blind people are there in our city?”

Birbal said, “I will find out, Your Majesty.”

The next day, Birbal sat in the market making charpoys (beds).

Many people passed by and asked, “What are you doing?”

Birbal wrote down their names.

Some people saw him clearly working, yet still asked the same question.

Later, Birbal presented the list to Akbar.

Akbar asked, “Why are these people called blind?”

Birbal said, “Because they could see me working, but still asked what I was doing.”

Akbar laughed and understood.

💖 Moral:

Those who do not observe carefully are like the blind.
